{"title":"Career Roadmap · HCI Researcher","role":"HCI Researcher","summary":"An HCI (Human-Computer Interaction) Researcher studies how people interact with computers, software, AI systems, interfaces, devices and emerging technologies, and uses research methods to design systems that are more usable, accessible, understandable and effective.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Human-Computer Interaction / Cognitive Computing"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An HCI (Human-Computer Interaction) Researcher studies how people interact with computers, software, AI systems, interfaces, devices and emerging technologies, and uses research methods to design systems that are more usable, accessible, understandable and effective."},{"type":"p","text":"With a specialization in Human-Computer Interaction / Cognitive Computing, the student should develop a hybrid profile combining:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computer science"},{"text":"Psychology and cognition"},{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Interaction design"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"UX research"},{"text":"AI/ML"},{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Prototyping"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role can involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Designing and conducting user studies"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Human-AI interaction research"},{"text":"Cognitive modelling"},{"text":"Interaction design evaluation"},{"text":"Eye-tracking and behavioural experiments"},{"text":"Accessibility research"},{"text":"Conversational-interface research"},{"text":"VR/AR interaction research"},{"text":"Multimodal interaction"},{"text":"Human-robot interaction"},{"text":"Academic research and publications"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential employers include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Universities and research laboratories"},{"text":"AI research organisations"},{"text":"Technology companies"},{"text":"UX research teams"},{"text":"Product companies"},{"text":"Healthcare technology companies"},{"text":"Automotive companies"},{"text":"Robotics companies"},{"text":"AR/VR companies"},{"text":"Government research institutions"},{"text":"Design and innovation labs"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus","Expected Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Research Foundation"},{"text":"Programming, psychology, UX, statistics, research methodology and HCI fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"HCI Researcher"},{"text":"User studies, experimentation, usability research, human-AI interaction"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior Researcher"},{"text":"Advanced HCI, cognitive systems, multimodal interaction, publications and research leadership"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Research Leadership"},{"text":"Principal Researcher, Research Scientist, HCI Lab Lead, Human-AI Interaction Strategist"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Tech/B.E.","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"HCI research is not simply UI/UX design."},{"type":"p","text":"A researcher needs to answer questions such as:"},{"type":"p","text":"Why do users behave this way?"},{"type":"p","text":"How does an interface affect cognition?"},{"type":"p","text":"Does an AI assistant improve decision-making?"},{"type":"p","text":"How does interaction design affect trust?"},{"type":"p","text":"Which interface produces better performance?"},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore, the student needs both technical and scientific research capabilities."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Computing + Human Behaviour Foundations"}]},{"heading":"Programming","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Primary recommendation:"},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"tex