AI Trust Study"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Cognitive Load Experiment"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Accessibility Study"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Multimodal Interaction Study"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Usability Evaluation"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Statistical Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Research Papers"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Conference Posters"}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certifications are less important here than research experience and demonstrable studies."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful learning areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HCI"},{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Cognitive Psychology"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Machine Learning"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Experimental Design"},{"text":"Scientific Writing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should prioritise:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research projects","publications","research internships","experiments"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"over collecting many generic certificates."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For an HCI Researcher, postgraduate education can be particularly valuable."},{"type":"p","text":"M.Tech / M.E."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HCI"},{"text":"Computer Science"},{"text":"AI/ML"},{"text":"Cognitive Computing"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Information Technology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"M.Sc."},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Cognitive Psychology"},{"text":"Computer Science"},{"text":"Data Science"},{"text":"Artificial Intelligence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"PhD"},{"type":"p","text":"For long-term research careers:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Computer Science"},{"text":"Human-AI Interaction"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Information Science"},{"text":"Robotics"},{"text":"Computational Social Science"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A PhD becomes especially relevant for university faculty and advanced research-scientist positions."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Human-AI Interaction Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI assistants"},{"text":"AI agents"},{"text":"Trust"},{"text":"Explainability"},{"text":"Human oversight"},{"text":"AI decision support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Cognitive Computing Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive modelling"},{"text":"Human reasoning"},{"text":"Machine cognition"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Intelligent systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. UX Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User behaviour"},{"text":"Product research"},{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"Product experimentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Human Factors Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human performance"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Cognitive workload"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"High-risk systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Accessibility Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Assistive technologies"},{"text":"Inclusive interfaces"},{"text":"Accessible AI"},{"text":"Universal design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Human-Robot Interaction Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Social robotics"},{"text":"Human-robot collaboration"},{"text":"Robot trust"},{"text":"Interaction models"}]},{"type":"h","text":"7. XR / Spatial Interaction Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"VR"},{"text":"AR"},{"text":"MR"},{"text":"Spatial computing"},{"text":"3D interfaces"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Route 1 — Academic Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E.","Research Assistant","M.Tech / M.Sc. HCI / Cognitive Science","PhD","Postdoctoral Researcher","Research Scientist / Faculty","Principal Investigator / HCI Lab Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route 2 — Industry Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E.","HCI / UX Research Assistant","HCI Researcher","Senior HCI Researcher","Principal Researcher","Research Lead / Research Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route 3 — Human-AI Interaction"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E.","AI / HCI Research Intern","Human-AI Interaction Researcher","Senior Researcher","Principal Human-AI Researcher","Human-AI Research Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route 4 — Research Engineering"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E.","Research Engineer","HCI / AI Research Engineer","Senior Research Engineer","Research Scientist","Principal Research Engineer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"The HCI field is increasingly moving beyond conventional graphical interfaces."},{"type":"p","text":"Key areas to monitor:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-AI interaction"},{"text":"AI agents"},{"text":"Conversational AI"},{"text":"Multimodal AI"},{"text":"Emotion-aware computing"},{"text":"Brain-computer interfaces"},{"text":"Spatial computing"},{"text":"AR/VR/MR"},{"text":"Human-robot interaction"},{"text":"Wearable computing"},{"text":"Ambient computing"},{"text":"Voice interfaces"},{"text":"Gesture interaction"},{"text":"Generative UI"},{"text":"Adaptive interfaces"},{"text":"Explainable AI"},{"text":"AI safety and human oversight"},{"text":"Accessible AI"},{"text":"Neuroadaptive interfaces"}]},{"type":"p","text":"One of the strongest future combinations is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["HCI","AI","Cognitive Science","Experimental Research"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"p","text":"HCI RESEARCHER"},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"p","text":"┌──────────────┼──────────────┐"},{"type":"p","text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"type":"p","text":"COMPUTER HUMAN RESEARCH"},{"type":"p","text":"SCIENCE SCIENCE METHODOLOGY"},{"type":"p","text":"│ │ │"},{"type":"p","text":"Python Psychology Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"ML Cognition Experiments"},{"type":"p","text":"Systems Behaviour Hypothesis"},{"type":"p","text":"AI Perception Evaluation"},{"type":"p","text":"│ │ │"},{"type":"flow","items":["└──────────────┼──────────────┘","HCI / UX"]},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"p","text":"┌──────────────┼──────────────┐"},{"type":"p","text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"type":"p","text":"Usability Interaction Accessibility"},{"type":"p","text":"Testing Design Research"},{"type":"p","text":"│ │ │"},{"type":"flow","items":["└──────────────┼──────────────┘","HUMAN-AI INTERACTION"]},{"type":"flow","items":["│","EXPERIMENTAL RESEARCH"]},{"type":"flow","items":["│","PAPERS / PROTOTYPES /"]},{"type":"p","text":"RESEARCH IMPACT"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By the end of B.Tech/B.E., the student should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Formulate an HCI research question"},{"text":"Conduct a structured literature review"},{"text":"Design a user experiment"},{"text":"Define hypotheses and variables"},{"text":"Recruit and study participants ethically"},{"text":"Build an interactive prototype"},{"text":"Conduct usability testing"},{"text":"Analyse quantitative data"},{"text":"Conduct qualitative analysis"},{"text":"Apply appropriate statistical methods"},{"text":"Evaluate AI-assisted interfaces"},{"text":"Understand cognitive principles"},{"text":"Build basic ML/AI systems"},{"text":"Design accessible interfaces"},{"text":"Write a research paper"},{"text":"Present research findings"},{"text":"Create reproducible research artefacts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate portfolio should contain 3–5 serious research projects, rather than a large collection of generic UI designs."},{"type":"h","text":"Research Workflow to Master"},{"type":"flow","items":["REAL-WORLD PROBLEM","Research Question","Literature Review","Hypothesis","Experimental Design","Prototype","User Study / Experiment","Data Collection","Statistical + Qualitative"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Analysis","Findings & Discussion","Limitations","Research Paper","Conference / Journal"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Tech/B.E. → Human-Computer Interaction / Cognitive Computing → HCI Researcher is best positioned as a research-intensive interdisciplinary career, combining computer science with psychology, cognition, statistics and interaction design."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["HCI","Cognitive Science","Statistics","UX Research","AI/ML","Human-AI Interaction","Experimental Design"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For an undergraduate, the highest-value differentiators are research methodology, statistics, user experimentation, strong HCI fundamentals, AI literacy, research internships and publications/research presentations. A master's or PhD becomes increasingly valuable if the goal is advanced industrial research or an academic/research-scientist career."}]}]}